{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Oboth.</b> Here they turned their faces northward, and the verse proves it, for in this encampment it is written אשר על פני מואב ממזרח השמש." "<b>And they encamped in Iyei-ha'avarim.</b> Rashi explained: the route of those who crossed there, by way of Mount Nevo into the land of Canaan. But according to what appears, Mount Nevo is not located there until after three encampments, as is specified in the section of Masei. And what Rashi further explained, that Mount Nevo separates between Moav and the Emorites — perhaps so it was before Sichon fought against the first king of Moav, but when he fought against him he took all his land from his hand, from Mount Nevo to the Arnon. Iyei-ha'avarim is like באי, with alef interchangeable with ayin."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:59.892448720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}